  "conclusion": "In this registry, Bamberg’s civic story concentrates around two lives that function like a cornerstone: Henry II’s institutional ambition and Cunigunde’s remembered virtue. Together they show how a city can be “founded” twice—first in policy and patronage, then again in memory, ritual, and the stories a community chooses to keep telling."
